+ Our Response to OpenAI's Claims, Live Webinar 
 ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌

Hi there,

Maddie here from Originality.AI!

Today we'd like to share a couple of newsworthy things happening in
the AI Content Detection world! 

* Our newest Case Study
that revealed
a 400% increase in the use of AI in Amazon Reviews

* Our comments on OpenAI's recent claims about Detection Efficacy 

**1. The Surge in AI-Generated Amazon Reviews**

We are excited to share the findings of our latest **case study**
, which
highlights a bit of a concerning trend!  We analyzed 2000 Amazon
Reviews and found the following: 

* 400% increase in AI generated review since the launch of Chat GPT

* Extreme reviews ( 1 star or 5 star reviews) are 1.3 times more likely
to be AI generated.

* Verified reviews are 1.4 times less likely to have AI Content

* Users Intuitively Find AI Generated Reviews Less Helpful

Would it make a difference to your purchasing decisions if you knew that
the review which persuaded you to purchase was actually AI Generated?

Read Full Study Here!

**2. Our Response to OpenAI on AI Detection**

Recently, OpenAI made a disappointing statement suggesting that AI
detectors do not effectively distinguish between AI-generated and
human-generated content. See below: 

**"Do AI Detectors work? In short, no. While some (including OpenAI)
have released tools that purport to detect AI-generated content, none of
these have proven to reliably distinguish between AI-generated and
human-generated content." -**

**OpenAI**

While we understand what OpenAI is attempting to communicate (no tool is
100% perfect with its detection), the reality is that detectors are very
much proven to be effective and the societal costs of AI content being
undetectable are too high for these simplified statements. 

This is not the first time that the AI detection sector has come under
fire, as the FTC has warned on multiple occasions against tools claiming
AI detection accuracy or unsubstantiated AI efficacy.  

**"If you're selling a tool that purports to detect generative AI
content, make sure that your claims accurately reflect the tool's
abilities and limitations."**- Federal Trade Commission

Originality.AI supports this view from the FTC and we have made it easy
for any company to test its own data to understand a detector's
efficacy.

We have Provided:

1.**A Detailed Study**
showing the
efficacy of our Detection 

2. An Open Sourced Data Set for transparency 

3. An **Open Sourced Tool**
to allow
researchers and customers alike to test AI detectors against various
datasets in order to determine the rate of AI detection and false
positives. 

Our Accuracy study
shows that
despite what OpenAI's statement suggests, AI detection can reliably be
accomplished. 

By suggesting that AI detection technology is not worth pursuing, OpenAI
is resigning us to a dark future where AI generated content is accepted
in the same pool as content created by real humans.

Have you done any of your own testing on our tool? If so, 

**reply to this email** and tell us about it! We'd love to learn more
about your testing process. 

****Reminder ****

**Sign up for our next LIVE WEBINAR to get the most out of our tool!**

During this webinar, our Amazing Customer Success Agent, Brady, will
help show you how to best utilize Originality.AI to get the most out of
it. 

This is a unique opportunity to engage with us directly and gain
valuable insights into Originality.AI best practices. 

To register yourself or your team for the webinar, simply click
below and secure your spot today. 

Register for Our Webinar

Thanks for reading! 

  

